      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/games/2026/nov/19/grand-theft-auto-six-fans-skip-work-pull-all-nighters",
      "description": "<p>Hotly anticipated Bonnie and Clyde-inspired adventure GTA VI has gamers glued to their screens around the world</p><p>Grand Theft Auto fans around the world pulled all-nighters, skipped work and school, and attended overnight launch parties to vicariously embark on police chases and coordinate robberies as the latest instalment of the eagerly anticipated series arrived.</p><p>GTA VI, a Bonnie and Clyde-inspired crime adventure game set in the fictional US state of Leonida, was launched at midnight on Wednesday after a 13-year wait.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/games/2026/nov/19/grand-theft-auto-six-fans-skip-work-pull-all-nighters\">Continue reading...</a>",
